{"subjectId":"cpp","id":"stringstream","title":"String Streams","group":"Errors, Streams & Utilities","order":67,"html":"<p class=\"lead\"><code>std::stringstream</code> (from <code>&lt;sstream&gt;</code>) is a stream whose buffer is a string — use it to parse text with <code>&gt;&gt;</code> or to build strings with <code>&lt;&lt;</code>.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-scan\"></i>Parsing</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;sstream&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n#include &lt;vector&gt;\n\nint main() {\n    std::istringstream in(\"3 4.5 hello 7\");\n    int a; double b; std::string word; int c;\n    in &gt;&gt; a &gt;&gt; b &gt;&gt; word &gt;&gt; c;\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; a + c &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; b &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; word &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n\n    std::string line = \"10,20,30\";\n    std::stringstream ss(line);\n    std::vector&lt;int&gt; nums;\n    for (std::string tok; std::getline(ss, tok, ',');) nums.push_back(std::stoi(tok));\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; nums.size() &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; nums[2] &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n\n    std::istringstream bad(\"12abc\");\n    int n; std::string rest;\n    bad &gt;&gt; n &gt;&gt; rest;                     // reads 12, then \"abc\"\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; n &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; rest &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n\n    std::istringstream words(\"  the   quick brown  \");\n    int count = 0;\n    for (std::string w; words &gt;&gt; w;) ++count;\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; count &lt;&lt; \" words\\n\";\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>10 4.5 hello\n3 30\n12 abc\n3 words</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-writing\"></i>Building strings</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iomanip&gt;\n#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;sstream&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n\nstd::string toHex(int value) {\n    std::ostringstream os;\n    os &lt;&lt; \"0x\" &lt;&lt; std::hex &lt;&lt; std::setw(4) &lt;&lt; std::setfill('0') &lt;&lt; value;\n    return os.str();\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::ostringstream report;\n    report &lt;&lt; \"total=\" &lt;&lt; 42 &lt;&lt; \", ratio=\" &lt;&lt; std::fixed &lt;&lt; std::setprecision(2) &lt;&lt; 0.4567;\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; report.str() &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; toHex(255) &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n\n    report.str(\"\");                        // reuse: reset the contents…\n    report.clear();                        // …and the state flags\n    report &lt;&lt; \"fresh\";\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; report.str() &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>total=42, ratio=0.46\n0x00ff\nfresh</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Direction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>std::istringstream</code></td><td>Read from a string (<code>&gt;&gt;</code>, <code>getline</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>std::ostringstream</code></td><td>Write into a string (<code>&lt;&lt;</code>, then <code>.str()</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>std::stringstream</code></td><td>Both</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>For simple number formatting <code>std::format</code> / <code>std::to_string</code> are faster and clearer; for fast number parsing without exceptions or locale, use <code>std::from_chars</code> (<code>&lt;charconv&gt;</code>).</p></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>How do you split a string by a delimiter in C++?</summary><div><p>Wrap it in a <code>std::stringstream</code> and call <code>std::getline(ss, token, delim)</code> in a loop — or, in C++20, iterate <code>str | std::views::split(delim)</code>. For whitespace-separated tokens, just use <code>ss &gt;&gt; token</code>.</p></div></details></section>"}